{"questions":[{"question_id":"1lfuqcf1v","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 1 Offline","year":2008,"examDate":2008,"subject":"physics","chapter":"current-electricity","chapterGroup":"electricity","topic":"meter-bridge","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pstatement-1p-pin-a-meter-bridge-experiment-null-p-jee-advanced-physics-motion-5sdsszs9tkefi8ju","content":"<p>STATEMENT - 1</p>\n<p>In a Meter Bridge experiment, null point for an unknown resistance is measured. Now, the unknown resistance is put inside an enclosure maintained at a higher temperature. The null point can be obtained at the same point as before by decreasing the value of the standard resistance.</p>\n<p>and</p>\n<p>STATEMENT - 2</p>\n<p>Resistance of a metal increases with increase in temperature.</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Statement - 1 is True, Statement - 2 is True; Statement - 2 is a correct explanation for Statement - 1"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement - 1 is True, Statement - 2 is True; Statement - 2 is NOT a correct explanation for Statement - 1"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Statement - 1 is True, Statement - 2 is False"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Statement - 1 is False, Statement - 2 is True"}],"correct_options":["D"],"explanation":"<p>When the temperature of a metal increases, its resistance will increase.</p>\n<p>Therefore statement-2 is correct.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lgkud1qx/84a999b0-8f1f-4552-b2cb-1c3c72090d54/7dc09090-dd1f-11ed-a69d-59b96e0d72fa/file-1lgkud1qy.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1lgkud1qx/84a999b0-8f1f-4552-b2cb-1c3c72090d54/7dc09090-dd1f-11ed-a69d-59b96e0d72fa/file-1lgkud1qy.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Current Electricity Question 7 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1lgkud1qx/84a999b0-8f1f-4552-b2cb-1c3c72090d54/7dc09090-dd1f-11ed-a69d-59b96e0d72fa/file-1lgkud1qy.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1lgkud1qx/84a999b0-8f1f-4552-b2cb-1c3c72090d54/7dc09090-dd1f-11ed-a69d-59b96e0d72fa/file-1lgkud1qy.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lgkud1qx/84a999b0-8f1f-4552-b2cb-1c3c72090d54/7dc09090-dd1f-11ed-a69d-59b96e0d72fa/file-1lgkud1qy.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1lgkud1qx/84a999b0-8f1f-4552-b2cb-1c3c72090d54/7dc09090-dd1f-11ed-a69d-59b96e0d72fa/file-1lgkud1qy.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1lgkud1qx/84a999b0-8f1f-4552-b2cb-1c3c72090d54/7dc09090-dd1f-11ed-a69d-59b96e0d72fa/file-1lgkud1qy.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1lgkud1qx/84a999b0-8f1f-4552-b2cb-1c3c72090d54/7dc09090-dd1f-11ed-a69d-59b96e0d72fa/file-1lgkud1qy.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>For meter bridge, when null point N is obtained, we get</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.912ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"10.492ex\" height=\"2.896ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -877 4637.5 1279.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D44B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(415.9,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g><rect width=\"802.5\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1320.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2376,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(862.4,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D445\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D445\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1500,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2278,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"2021.5\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>When the unknown resistance is put inside an enclosure, maintained at a high temperature, then X increases. To maintain the ratio of null point, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.674ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 298 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> should also increase. But if we want to keep the null point at the initial position (i.e., if we want to change the value of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.674ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 298 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) to maintain the ratio, R should be increased.</p>\n<p>Therefore, statement - 1 is false.</p>"}]}